--- parity notes (web source: features/system/components/CommandTile.tsx, 84 lines) ---
* Presentational tile: clickable GlassPanel (cursor-pointer, opacity-50 while loading) -> centered
  [ neutral icon box(40dp, rounded-xl == Radius.md, surface-2 == surfaceVariant; Loader2 -> CircularProgressIndicator
  while loading, else def.icon at 20dp) + label(text-xs medium onSurface, 2-line) + optional sublabel(text-[10px]
  muted) + optional lastStatus(text-[9px], green/red by leading checkmark) ]; favourite Star pinned top-start;
  AlertTriangle pinned top-end when dangerous.
* handleClick precedence reproduced 1:1 by CommandTileClickResolver: loading -> Ignore; dangerous -> RequestDialog
  (host confirm dialog); else -> Execute(def.command, def.params). Unit-tested incl. loading-over-dangerous order.
* lastStatus tone reproduced by CommandStatusTone.fromStatus: null/blank -> None (web {lastStatus &&}); leading
  U+2713 -> Success (status.success); else -> Error (status.danger). Variant default/danger/success ->
  CommandVariant + GlassPanel accent (None/Danger/Success); dark tokens == web neon hexes.
* Hook-less surface (web only binds useTranslation). Per the ToolCard/QuickNav precedent, NO loading/empty/error/
  stale/offline DATA lifecycle is invented (would be drift) - those live on the owning Commands page. The genuine
  source render branches (loading vs idle, favourite on/off, dangerous on/off, success/error/no status, sublabel
  present/absent, 3 variants) are all reproduced and exercised by the UI + unit tests.
* i18n (P1/S10): the surface's own key commands.toggleFavorite resolves via R.string.translation_commands_toggleFavorite;
  the loading state-description uses R.string.translation_a11y_loading. Per-command label/sublabel arrive already-
  localized on CommandTileDef (the native home of the web t(def.labelKey) dynamic-key lookup). No English literals shipped.
* Telemetry (P1/S11): stateful CommandTile emits view.opened {surface: "CommandTile"} via the redacting Logger; slug-only.
* a11y: tile is Role.Button (label text is its readable name; busy state-description while loading); favourite IconButton
  carries the 'Toggle favorite' contentDescription + 48dp target and consumes its own taps (web e.stopPropagation());
  icon box, spinner and warning triangle are decorative (null contentDescription, web sets no aria-label on the triangle).
* Star glyph authored locally (filled + outline, lucide parity) as Android ships no lucide; AlertTriangle reuses the
  shared TeslaGlyphs.Warning. Capability present: Kotlin 2.4.0 / AGP 8.9.2 / Compose BOM 2026.04.01 / Material 3 (>= the
  prompt's Compose+M3+Kotlin-2.x minimum), JDK 21, Gradle 8.14.5 - assembleRelease + testReleaseUnitTest both green.

